{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "event_id": "fe30568a-7b27-4232-9246-9103165caf9f", "run_id": "D002", "seq": 3, "ts": "2026-10-23T21:44:18.988Z", "type": "prompt", "actor": "human", "phase": "constitution", "condition": "sdd", "task_id": "T-LOGIN-01", "session_id": null, "payload": {"text": "/speckit-constitution Establish the constitution for a small Python project. Principles: (1) Standard library only - no third-party runtime dependencies; (2) Fail loudly - invalid input produces a clear message and a non-zero exit status or an error response, never a silent wrong answer; (3) Every requirement is testable - each functional requirement maps to at least one automated pytest test; (4) Simplicity - the smallest design that meets the specification.\n", "chars": 464, "words": 70, "sha256": "5d93067ea6ef2e343310e5fc3bd556951b07039188bcbbd63b7a27f0dde77ed4", "source": "manual"}}
